  "analysis": "We need to implement a solution to the Bribes problem. The roads form a tree with some edges directed (a -> b) and some bidirectional (a <-> b). The lorry starts at town 1 and must visit s1, s2, ..., sK in order. When traversing an edge in the forbidden direction (i.e., against its allowed direction, for directed edges only), a bribe is paid. The total bribe across all traversals on an edge e with t reverse traversals is 1000 * (2^t - 1). Since the output expects the total in thousands of Ruritanian dinars modulo 1e9+7, we sum (2^t - 1) over all edges with t reverse traversals and take mod 1e9+7. Key observations: for each consecutive pair (u, v), the path is unique on the tree; edges on the path from u up to LCA(u, v) are traversed upwards, edges on the path from LCA to v are traversed downwards. We can accumulate for each edge how many times it is traversed upwards (upCnt) and downwards (downCnt) across all pairs using a pair of path-difference arrays, one counting the upward portions and one counting the downward portions. Then for each edge with X=1 (directed), if its orientation is parent->child, t = upCnt; if orientation is child->parent, t = downCnt; sum (2^t - 1) over edges with t > 0, modulo 1e9+7. We implement LCA with binary lifting, perform O(K log N) LCA computations for K up to 1e6, and accumulate counts in O(N). Finally, precompute powers of two up to K for efficient modulo arithmetic. The approach satisfies constraints N ≤ 1e5, K ≤ 1e6 and runs efficiently in time. ",
  "plan": "Steps to implement:\n1) Read N and the N-1 edges, build an undirected adjacency with edge ids, store A[i], B[i], X[i].\n2) Root the tree at 1 using BFS to compute depth[], parent[], and parEdge[] (edge to parent) for each node.\n3) Build binary lifting table up[LOG][N+1] for LCA. Implement LCA(u,v).\n4) Read K and the sequence s[0..K-1]. Initialize two arrays upAdd[] and downAdd[] of size N+1 to zero.\n5) For i from 0 to K-2, compute w = LCA(s[i], s[i+1]); do upAdd[s[i]]++, upAdd[w]--, and downAdd[s[i+1]]++, downAdd[w]--.\n6) Compute edge counts in a bottom-up fashion by processing nodes in decreasing depth order. For each node u ≠ 1, let p = parent[u], e = parEdge[u]; set upCnt[e] = upAdd[u], downCnt[e] = downAdd[u]; then accumulate upAdd[p] += upAdd[u] and downAdd[p] += downAdd[u].\n7) Precompute powers of two modulo MOD up to K+4 (to cover 2^t where t ≤ K-1).\n8) For every edge e (1..N-1) with X[e] = 1, determine whether its allowed direction is p->c or c->p using depths to identify child c and parent p. If A[e]==p and B[e]==c, t = upCnt[e]; if A[e]==c and B[e]==p, t = downCnt[e]. Add (2^t - 1) to answer if t > 0. All arithmetic modulo 1e9+7.\n9) Print the final answer modulo MOD.\n\nEdge cases: K=1 => no transitions; answer 0. Edges with X=0 contribute 0 regardless of counts.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "bash -lc 'cat > main.cpp <<\"CPP\"\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\n\nint main(){\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int N; if(!(cin>>N)) return 0; int M = N-1;\n    vector<int> A(M+1), B(M+1), X(M+1);\n    vector<vector<pair<int,int>>> adj(N+1);\n    for(int i=1;i<=M;++i){\n        int a,b,x; cin>>a>>b>>x; A[i]=a; B[i]=b; X[i]=x; adj[a].push_back({b,i}); adj[b].push_back({a,i});\n    }\n    int K; cin>>K; vector<int> s(K); for(int i=0;i<K;++i) cin>>s[i];\n\n    // BFS from 1 to set depth, parent, parEdge\n    vector<int> depth(N+1,0), parent(N+1,0), parEdge(N+1,-1);\n    vector<char> vis(N+1,false);\n    queue<int> q; q.push(1); vis[1]=true; parent[1]=0; depth[1]=0;\n    while(!q.empty()){\n        int u=q.front(); q.pop();\n        for(auto &e: adj[u]){\n            int v=e.first; int eid=e.second;\n            if(!vis[v]){ vis[v]=true; parent[v]=u; parEdge[v]=eid; depth[v]=depth[u]+1; q.push(v); }\n        }\n    }\n\n    int LOG = 1; while((1<<LOG) <= N) LOG++;\n    vector<vector<int>> up(LOG, vector<int>(N+1,0));\n    for(int v=1; v<=N; ++v) up[0][v] = parent[v];\n    for(int k=1;k<LOG;++k){\n        for(int v=1; v<=N; ++v){\n            int mid = up[k-1][v]; up[k][v] = mid ? up[k-1][mid] : 0;\n        }\n    }\n    auto lca = [&](int a,int b)->int{\n        if (depth[a] < depth[b]) swap(a,b);\n        int diff = depth[a]-depth[b];\n        for(int k=0;k<LOG;++k) if (diff & (1<<k)) a = up[k][a];\n        if (a==b) return a;\n        for(int k=LOG-1; k>=0; --k){\n            if (up[k][a] != up[k][b]){ a = up[k][a]; b = up[k][b]; }\n        }\n        return parent[a];\n    };\n\n    vector<long long> upAdd(N+1,0), downAdd(N+1,0);\n    for(int i=0;i<K-1;++i){\n        int u = s[i], v = s[i+1]; int w = lca(u,v);\n        upAdd[u] += 1; upAdd[w] -= 1;\n        downAdd[v] += 1; downAdd[w] -= 1;\n    }\n\n    // Process nodes in decreasing depth to accumulate counts bottom-up\n    vector<int> nodes(N); for(int i=0;i<N;++i) nodes[i]=i+1;\n    sort(nodes.begin(), nodes.end(), [&](int a,int b){ return depth[a] > depth[b]; });\n    vector<long long> upCnt(M+1,0), downCnt(M+1,0);\n    for(int idx=0; idx<N; ++idx){\n        int u = nodes[idx];\n        if (u==1) continue;\n        int p = parent[u]; int e = parEdge[u];\n        upCnt[e] = upAdd[u];\n        downCnt[e] = downAdd[u];\n        upAdd[p] += upAdd[u];\n        downAdd[p] += downAdd[u];\n    }\n\n    // Precompute powers of two up to K+4\n    vector<long long> pow2(K+5);\n    pow2[0] = 1;\n    for(size_t i=1;i<pow2.size(); ++i) pow2[i] = (pow2[i-1]*2) % MOD;\n\n    long long ans = 0;\n    for(int e=1; e<=M; ++e){\n        if (X[e] == 0) continue; // bidirectional, no bribe\n        int a = A[e], b = B[e];\n        int c = (depth[a] > depth[b]) ? a : b; // child\n        int p = (c==a) ? b : a;               // parent\n        long long t = 0;\n        if (a==p && b==c){ // allowed direction is p -> c (downwards)\n            t = upCnt[e];\n        } else if (a==c && b==p){ // allowed direction is c -> p (upwards)\n            t = downCnt[e];\n        } else {\n            t = 0; // should not happen for a valid edge in a tree\n        }\n        if (t > 0) {\n            ans = (ans + (pow2[(int)t] - 1 + MOD) % MOD) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << ans % MOD << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\nCPP'\n"
